// Predators & Stealth -- PalSchema aggression patch. Hand-edit freely; restart the game after.
// Retune a category with find & replace -- HearingRate (heard m): 16.0 sharp-eared | 10.0 default | 6.0 deaf.
// Knobs per pal: AIResponse (hostility) | ViewingDistance (aggro/sight m, flat 25) | HearingRate (heard m).
// AIResponse tags: Warlike | Warlike_Anyway | NotInterested | Escape | Friendly | (Kill_All/Boss avoid).
// ALL species are "Warlike" (2026-08-05). WHY plain Warlike, not the old blanket "Warlike_Anyway":
//   "Warlike_Anyway" ignores the biological-GRADE check entirely -- so a weak pal will suicide-charge
//   anything, and the whole world brawls (pals attack each other, not just you). Plain "Warlike" keeps
//   the grade check (a pal won't engage something it reads as far stronger), which kills the inter-pal
//   chaos. The one thing plain Warlike breaks is MOUNTED aggro (mounted, wild pals read your MOUNT's
//   grade, which is > your 0, so they stand down) -- and that is now fixed in CODE, not data:
//   Scripts/mount_aggro.lua pins the ridden pal's grade to 0 while you ride (confirmed live via the
//   grade probe). The per-line "(Escape_to_Battle -> ...)" notes just record originally-escape species;
//   if any of THOSE still won't commit on foot under plain Warlike, give only those "Warlike_Anyway".
// Sight is a flat 25 for all -- no level/threat scaling (see MODPAGE for why). Tune per pal if you want.
// Prey (passive) = the species simply ABSENT from this file.
{
  "DT_PalMonsterParameter": {
    "BadCatgirl": { "AIResponse": "Warlike", "ViewingDistance": 25, "HearingRate": 16.0 }, // sharp ears
